<title>TURKEY: TURK EREGLI SIGNS 2-YR LABOUR CONTRACT.</title>
<headline>TURK EREGLI SIGNS 2-YR LABOUR CONTRACT.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's leading flat steel producer Eregli Demir ve Celik Fabrikalari T.A.S. signed a two-year labour contract with Turk Metal Union, representing 4,200 workers, the union said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>A union official told Reuters that the hourly wage would be increased by 40 percent for the first six months and 31 percent for the second six months.</p>
<p>According to the agreement, wage increases every six months will be indexed to inflation for the second year. Turkey's 1996 consumer inflation was 79.8 percent.</p>
<p>There will be 92 percent rise in fringe benefits, the official said.</p>
<p>The agreement will be retroactive from September 1, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
